## Quote Generator UI Redesign

Today, I continued improving the Quote Generator application with a focus on making the interface feel more polished, modern, and closer to a professional SaaS product.

### What I worked on
Redesigned the navigation to use a full-width layout with a cleaner and more spacious structure.
Updated the overall interface to follow a minimal SaaS design direction, inspired by the provided pricing-page reference.
Improved the visual hierarchy of the Quote Generator while keeping the existing functionality intact.
Added a subscription pricing experience with a $5/month Premium plan.
Designed a pricing modal that appears 10 seconds after a user enters the application.
Made the pricing modal appear only once per browser session to avoid repeatedly interrupting the user.
Added a fixed Premium banner that appears above the navigation when the user cancels the pricing modal.
Added the ability for users to click "View plans" on the banner to reopen the pricing modal.
Made the pricing experience responsive for desktop and mobile.
Updated the New Quote button from an outlined style to a filled lime-green CTA, making it more visually prominent.
Added hover, active, and accessibility states to the New Quote button.
Ensured the existing quote-generation, authentication, saved quotes, categories, sharing, and other core functionality remain intact.
